  - [1mResponse missing [38;5;153muserId[0m — refuse to store a partial identity instead of persisting [38;5;153mundefined[39m.

  And the standing constraint from your "label only" answer, which I'll write into the spec as a rule: [1mnothing may [0m
  [1mauthorize on this value.[0m It's for logs and form payloads.

  [1m4. Tooling[0m

  Vitest plus ESLint and Prettier, with [38;5;153mtest[39m / [38;5;153mlint[39m / [38;5;153mformat[39m scripts, and a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m (the repo has none, and we're
  about to create [38;5;153mnode_modules[39m).

  One trap worth naming: I will [1mnot[0m set [38;5;153m"type": "module"[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. That's the obvious way to make ESM work, and
  it would silently break [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m and [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m, which use [38;5;153mrequire[39m. Vitest handles ESM without it, and browsers
  ignore [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m entirely.

  [1m5. What this costs you[0m

  Opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking stops working — module scripts need a real origin. [38;5;153mnpx serve .[39m or [38;5;153mpython3 -m [39m
  [38;5;153mhttp.server[39m covers it. That's the one user-visible regression in this change.

  [1mAssumption to validate:[0m that the real login API will return a stable, server-assigned [38;5;153muserId[39m field. Nothing in the
  repo confirms the response shape, since [38;5;153mlogin()[39m never calls [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m. I'll record it as an assumption in the spec
  rather than as a fact.
